<article class="env-lemma" id="064D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/064D">Lemma <span data-tag="064D">13.19.10</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Let $P^\bullet $, $K^\bullet $ be complexes. Let $n \in \mathbf{Z}$. Assume that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$P^\bullet $ is a bounded complex consisting of projective objects, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$P^ i = 0$ for $i < n$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$H^ i(K^\bullet ) = 0$ for $i \geq n$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{K(\mathcal{A})}(P^\bullet , K^\bullet ) = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{D(\mathcal{A})}(P^\bullet , K^\bullet ) = 0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The first equality follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/064B" data-tag="064B">13.19.8</a>. Note that there is a distinguished triangle 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  (\tau _{\leq n - 1}K^\bullet , K^\bullet , \tau _{\geq n}K^\bullet , f, g, h)  \]
</div>
    <p>
       by Remark <a href="/tag/08J5" data-tag="08J5">13.12.4</a>. Hence, by Lemma <a href="/tag/0149" data-tag="0149">13.4.2</a> it suffices to prove $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{K(\mathcal{A})}(P^\bullet , \tau _{\leq n - 1}K^\bullet ) = 0$ and $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{K(\mathcal{A})}(P^\bullet , \tau _{\geq n} K^\bullet ) = 0$. The first vanishing is trivial and the second is Lemma <a href="/tag/0647" data-tag="0647">13.19.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>